WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.400
She-Hulk fans, rejoice: the rumor mill may
have given us a clue as to when Jennifer Walters

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.960
will finally appear the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:13.080
Sources close to Cosmic Book News have indicated
that Marvel may be looking at the third solo

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.910
Spider-Man film to introduce the character
and while this is little more than speculation

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.180
for now, there are a couple of factors working
in the rumor's favour.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.680
First, there's an offhand remark that Spider-Man:
Far From Home star Tom Holland made a couple

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:26.500
months back in an interview with Fandom.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.019
Holland was bandying about the names of several
interesting characters whom he'd like to one

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:35.760
day see in the MCU, from Nick Fury, Jr. to
Riri Williams, also known as Ironheart.

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.090
But in the middle of all this, Holland took
time out to explain that he'd love to see

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:42.160
Spidey team up with Mark Ruffalo's Hulk in
a future adventure.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.060
Holland explained:

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.360
"[Hulk] is so funny, and they're both science
geeks."

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:49.860
And while Jennifer Walters isn't quite the
same character as Bruce Banner, an appearance

00:00:49.879 --> 00:00:54.440
by Hulk in Spider-Man 3 could easily set up
the introduction of Walters, who in the comics

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:55.540
is Banner's cousin.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.720
"Best of both worlds."

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.559
More interesting, however, is the alleged
plot that Marvel is cooking up for the third

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:03.640
solo Spidey outing.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.200
Although you'll need to take this with a healthy
dose of salt, Cosmic Book News reports that

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:13.170
YouTuber TVO has the skinny straight from
inside sources that the plot of Marvel's third

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:17.220
Spider-Man flick will follow directly from
Far From Home's mid-credits sequence, in which

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:22.440
blowhard vlogger J. Jonah Jameson publicly
reveals doctored footage making it appear

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:27.360
as if Spidey, not Mysterio, had been to blame
for the staged elemental attacks on various

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:28.460
European locales.

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:32.380
In fact, this footage even puts Spidey on
the hook for straight-up killing Mysterio

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:36.770
and the villain, with his supposed dying breath,
reveals the web-slinger's secret identity

00:01:36.770 --> 00:01:37.400
to the world.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:41.660
According to TVO's sources, the third flick
will see Peter Parker attempting to clear

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:44.700
his name through the proper channels, that
is, the legal system.

00:01:44.740 --> 00:01:48.740
Apparently, the idea was put forth that acting
as Parker's defense attorney would be none

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:53.570
other than Matt Murdock, also known as Daredevil,
a situation for which there is ample precedent

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:54.240
in the comics.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:57.540
"And I'm a Catholic - I have a soft spot for hopeless
causes."

00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.800
Unfortunately, that plot would be tricky to
pull off.

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:05.840
As part of the deal struck between Netflix
and Marvel, reportedly none of the characters

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:09.670
who appeared in the streamer's now-defunct
slate of Marvel series are eligible for use

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:14.400
in the MCU until two full years after each
respective series' cancellation.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:18.200
That means that Marvel Studios would have
to wait for a while before bringing Murdock

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:19.780
into play in any capacity.

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:23.680
Rather than deal with the possibility of having
to adjust the timetable for production on

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.010
the next Spidey flick, Marvel's brain trust
simply defaulted to the next most well-known

00:02:28.010 --> 00:02:30.560
attorney in all of Marvel lore Walters.

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:35.020
In the comics, hotshot lawyer Jennifer Walters
is shot and seriously injured by a vengeful

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:36.680
gangster while in town for a visit.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:40.980
She receives a blood transfusion from dear
cousin Bruce, leading to Walters becoming

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:41.940
the savage She-Hulk.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.330
The character has gone through quite an evolution
since she first debuted; as she retains her

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:51.060
intellect and personality post-transformation,
she even eventually decides to just remain

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.480
Hulked out permanently, even in the course
of her day job as a defense lawyer.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:58.620
Although TVO's sources didn't let on as to
whether Walters would appear in her She-Hulk

00:02:58.629 --> 00:03:02.780
persona during the film, there's something
to be said for the idea of Parker being represented

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.200
in court by a giant, green superhero lawyer.

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:09.200
At any rate, it's important to reiterate that
this is an unverified rumor.

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.780
Still, it would be a pretty cool way to introduce
Walters into an MCU that could sorely use

00:03:13.790 --> 00:03:18.400
a new Hulk especially now that Banner is probably
undergoing intensive physical therapy after

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.651
that whole Infinity Gauntlet thing went down.

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:22.120
That looked like it hurt.

